DevOps Interview Command Series — Git (Day 3) 🌱

Git is the heart of DevOps workflows.
From CI/CD pipelines to Infrastructure as Code and team collaboration — everything starts with Git.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Git commands you must know:

git --version
git config --global user.name "name"
git config --global user.email "email"

git init
git clone repo_url
git status

git add .
git commit -m "message"
git log --oneline
git show

git branch
git branch feature-branch
git checkout branch
git checkout -b new-branch

git pull
git fetch
git push origin branch

git diff
git reset --soft HEAD~1
git reset --hard HEAD~1

git stash
git stash pop

git merge branch
git rebase branch

git remote -v
git tag


🎯 Interview Focus
• Resolve merge conflicts
• Roll back faulty commits
• Maintain clean branch strategy
• Understand rebase vs merge
• Handle CI failures due to Git mistakes
